Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:04:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] iio: adc: sun4i-gpadc: unregister the thermal zone with
 the IIO device
To: Jonathan Cameron <jic23@kernel.org>,
    Rafael J. Wysocki <rafael@kernel.org>,
    Daniel Lezcano <daniel.lezcano@kernel.org>
Cc: David Lechner <dlechner@baylibre.com>,
    Nuno Sá <nuno.sa@analog.com>,
    Andy Shevchenko <andy@kernel.org>,
    Chen-Yu Tsai <wens@kernel.org>,
    Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>,
    Samuel Holland <samuel@sholland.org>,
    Zhang Rui <rui.zhang@intel.com>,
    Lukasz Luba <lukasz.luba@arm.com>,
    linux-iio@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-pm@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-sunxi@lists.linux.dev,
    linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

On the A10, A13, A20 and A31 the IIO device is a child of the
sun4i-gpadc MFD, and the thermal zone is registered for the parent
device, whose DT node holds the sensor. Since the conversion to the new
OF thermal API it is registered with devm_thermal_of_zone_register() on
that parent, so it stays registered when the IIO driver is unbound or
unloaded, with ops and devdata pointing to the freed driver.

Unloading and reloading the module on an A10 board oopses in the
thermal workqueue a second later (the new zone shows up as
thermal_zone1 next to the stale thermal_zone0):

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000002c when read
  PC is at sun4i_gpadc_get_temp+0x36/0x64 [sun4i_gpadc_iio]
  Workqueue: thermal_events thermal_zone_device_check
   sun4i_gpadc_get_temp [sun4i_gpadc_iio] from __thermal_zone_get_temp+0x11/0x3c
   __thermal_zone_get_temp from __thermal_zone_device_update+0x71/0x3d8

Commit 82237f268281 ("iio: adc: sun4i-gpadc-iio: fix parent device
being used in devm function") fixed this once by unregistering the zone
in .remove(); the conversion dropped that. The zone cannot simply be
registered for the IIO device, as devm_thermal_of_zone_register() takes
the sensor node from the device it is given. Release the parent's zone
with a devm action on the IIO device instead, which also covers the
probe error path. The zone now goes after .remove() rather than at its
start; a temperature read in between fails cleanly, as runtime PM is
already disabled. In DT mode the zone already belongs to the IIO device.

Tested on an A10 board (Rikomagic MK802): four unload/reload cycles
without an oops (with the whole series applied); the zone goes away with
the module and comes back with it.

Fixes: de15b8403fa9 ("iio/drivers/sun4i_gpadc: Switch to new of thermal API")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c b/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c
index ac5ba76b979..420b921849a 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c
@@ -595,6 +595,13 @@ static int sun4i_gpadc_probe_mfd(struct platform_device *pdev,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void sun4i_gpadc_unregister_tz(void *data)
+{
+	struct sun4i_gpadc_iio *info = data;
+
+	devm_thermal_of_zone_unregister(info->sensor_device, info->tzd);
+}
+
 static int sun4i_gpadc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct sun4i_gpadc_iio *info;
@@ -643,6 +650,19 @@ static int sun4i_gpadc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 					    "could not register thermal sensor\n");
 			goto err_map;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * In MFD mode the zone is registered for the parent device,
+		 * whose DT node holds the sensor, so devres would keep it
+		 * until the parent goes away. Unregister it with this device.
+		 */
+		if (!IS_ERR(info->tzd) && info->sensor_device != &pdev->dev) {
+			ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(&pdev->dev,
+						       sun4i_gpadc_unregister_tz,
+						       info);
+			if (ret)
+				goto err_map;
+		}
 	}
 
 	ret = devm_iio_device_register(&pdev->dev, indio_dev);
-- 
